    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nThe comment textobj mapping does not work, despite the mapping being correctly created.\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-979+g794981d9b\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nConfiguration used:\r\n```\r\n\tconfig = function()\r\n\t\trequire('mini.comment').setup {\r\n\t\t\tmappings = {\r\n\t\t\t\tcomment = ';;',\r\n\t\t\t\tcomment_line = ';;',\r\n\t\t\t\ttextobject = ';',\r\n\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t}\r\n\tend\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutput of `omap`:\r\n```\r\no  ;           * <Cmd>lua MiniComment.textobject()<CR>\r\n```\r\n\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nUsing <kbd>;</kbd><kbd>;</kbd> in normal/visual mode works, but <kbd>c</kbd><kbd>i</kbd><kbd>;</kbd>, for example, fails.",
